@layout.app({ title: 'Privacy Policy' })
  @slot('meta')
    <meta name="description" content="How nvp.gg collects, uses, and keeps your information." />
  @endslot
  
  <div class="ember-primitives__hero__wrapper">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1>
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <em>Last updated: September 21, 2026</em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="legal">
    <p>
      nvp.gg is a URL shortener. This policy explains what information we collect when you use it,
      why we collect it, and what we do with it. We keep it short because we collect little.
    </p>

    <p>
      Our principles:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We only ask for information we need to run the service.
      </li>
      <li>
        We keep information only as long as we have a reason to keep it.
      </li>
      <li>
        We do not sell your information, and we do not run ads or third-party analytics.
      </li>
      <li>
        We say plainly who else sees your information and why.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="scope">
      Who we are and what this policy covers
    </h2>
    <p>
      nvp.gg is run by NullVoxPopuli. This policy applies to information we collect when you use
      nvp.gg, api.nvp.gg, docs.nvp.gg, and any short link served by them. Together we call these
      the "Service".
    </p>
    <p>
      When you visit a short link, the site it sends you to has its own privacy policy. That site is
      not covered here.
    </p>

    <h2 id="information-we-collect">
      Information we collect
    </h2>

    <h3>
      Information you give us
    </h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong>
        You sign in with GitHub. GitHub sends us your GitHub
        user id, your display name, and an access token. We store all three. We do not store your
        email address or your password.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account and team names.</strong>
        The name of your account, the names of any team
        accounts you create, and the invitations you send.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Links.</strong>
        Every long URL you shorten, the short code we assign, when you made
        it, when it expires, and any custom domain you attach.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Custom domains.</strong>
        The hostnames you add to your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>API keys.</strong>
        The name, scopes, and expiry of each key. We store a hash of the
        key, not the key itself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Payment information.</strong>
        Stripe handles payment. Your card number never
        reaches our servers. We store the Stripe customer id, the subscription status and period,
        the card brand, and the last four digits of the card.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>
      Information we collect automatically
    </h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Link visits.</strong>
        When someone opens a short link, we record the time, the
        referring page, and the browser's user agent string. We do not store the visitor's IP
        address. Visit counts appear on your dashboard.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Session cookie.</strong>
        When you sign in, we set a cookie that keeps you signed in.
        It is the only cookie we set.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs.</strong>
        Our hosting provider keeps standard web server logs, which
        include IP addresses, for a short time for security and debugging.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>
      Information from other sources
    </h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub.</strong>
        The account information above, when you sign in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stripe.</strong>
        Subscription and payment events, so we know what plan you are on.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how-we-use-information">
      How and why we use information
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>To run the Service.</strong>
        To keep you signed in, serve your short links, count visits, and enforce plan limits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To bill you.</strong>
        To start, renew, change, and cancel a paid plan through Stripe.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To protect the Service.</strong>
        To detect abuse, spam, malware links, and security incidents, and to meet our legal obligations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To fix problems.</strong>
        To debug errors and keep the Service up.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To contact you.</strong>
        Only about your account, such as a change to these terms or a problem with a link. We do not send marketing.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, our legal bases are: the
      contract we have with you when you use the Service, our legitimate interest in running and
      protecting it, and our legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sharing-information">
      Sharing information
    </h2>
    <p>
      We share information only in these cases:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Stripe</strong>, to process payments and manage subscriptions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub</strong>, to sign you in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our hosting provider</strong>, which stores the database and serves the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal requests.</strong>
        If a subpoena, court order, or other lawful request requires it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To protect people.</strong>
        If we believe in good faith that sharing is needed to prevent harm, fraud, or abuse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Team members.</strong>
        Members of a team account can see the links, domains, and visit counts of that account, and the names of the other members.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>With your consent.</strong>
        When you ask us to.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Short links are public by design. Anyone with a short link can open it and reach the long
      URL. Visit counts are visible only to the account that owns the link.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">
      How long we keep information
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Account information stays while your account exists.
      </li>
      <li>
        A link and its visit records stay until you delete the link, the link expires, or you close your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        Stripe records stay as long as tax and accounting law require, after which we delete what we hold.
      </li>
      <li>
        Hosting provider logs are kept for about 30 days.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Backups can hold deleted data for a short time after deletion.
    </p>

    <h2 id="security">
      Security
    </h2>
    <p>
      No online service is fully secure. We use HTTPS everywhere, store API keys as hashes, keep
      card data out of our systems, and limit who can reach the database.
    </p>

    <h2 id="choices">
      Your choices
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Delete any link from your dashboard. Its visit records go with it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Revoke any API key from your dashboard.
      </li>
      <li>
        Cancel a paid plan at any time through the billing portal.
      </li>
      <li>
        Close your account by contacting us. We delete your account, links, and visit records.
      </li>
      <li>
        Reject cookies in your browser. You will not be able to sign in.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="your-rights">
      Your rights
    </h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you can have the right to access, correct, export, or delete
      the information we hold about you, or to object to how we use it. Contact us and we will
      act on the request. If we refuse, we will say why, and you can complain to your local data
      protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">
      Children
    </h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not for children. You must be at least 13 years old, or 16 in the European
      Economic Area, to use it. We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you
      believe a child gave us information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="transfers">
      Where information is stored
    </h2>
    <p>
      The Service runs on servers in the United States. If you use it from elsewhere, your
      information moves to the United States.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">
      Changes to this policy
    </h2>
    <p>
      We can change this policy. When we do, we update the date at the top. If a change is
      material, we will also say so on the site. Your continued use after a change means you
      accept it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">
      How to reach us
    </h2>
    <p>
      Open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/NullVoxPopuli/url-shortener">GitHub</a>
      or ask in the Discord linked in the footer.
    </p>

    <p class="attribution">
      Adapted from
      <a href="https://github.com/Automattic/legalmattic">Automattic's Legalmattic</a>
      privacy policy, under the
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">Creative Commons BY-SA 4.0</a>
      license. This policy is available under the same license.
    </p>
  </main>
@end
